title ALES142 — Lotus's stereo_soft_center_clip: the soft center clipper carried into stereo, the continuous dead zone that holds phase yet breaks ratio
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Second lap of this recur turn (after ALES141 stereo_center_clip). The ALES141 log named the rest of the dead-zone family as a mechanical kg continuation; crux-first, I took ALES88's soft center clipper next, the continuous twin of the hard center clip just lifted. It teaches a richer contrast than a plain repeat: where ALES141 held BOTH ratio and antisymmetry and was idempotent, the soft form holds only the antisymmetry.
think ALES88's soft_center_clip is y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else x − sign(x)·t — silence the dead zone, then shift every survivor toward zero by exactly t, so the survivor rises continuously from zero (|x| = t+1 → ±1). It is ODD (sign flips with the sign), so carried into stereo it HOLDS the inter-channel antisymmetry: an out-of-phase master stays out of phase. Yet it is a SHIFT, not a mask, and a shift is not scale-invariant, so it BREAKS the inter-channel ratio (2x − t ≠ 2(x − t)); and it is NOT idempotent (each pass subtracts t again). I proved all three honestly: antisymmetry held (r[i] = −l[i]), ratio broken (asserted 2·l[0] ≠ r[0] on a 1:2 master where both survive), not idempotent (asserted twice ≠ once). Stated the honest edges plainly rather than dressing the shift in symmetries it lacks.
think The round's family bond is the SOFT/HARD BOND read in stereo: both dead-zone members silence the SAME dead zone, and on every survivor |soft| = |hard| − t. Imported ALES141's stereo_center_clip and proved the bond per channel per sample — a first cross-module witness dependency on the rung I built last lap (mirrors ALES140 importing stereo_halve for the family-whole law). The lift itself is the seated pattern: run ALES88's mono soft_center_clip per channel with one shared threshold, validated once up front (BadThreshold, BadRange); SoftCenterClipError reused whole.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local software, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. The stereo dead-zone corner now holds a hard/soft pair, exactly as the DRIVE family carries hard-clip/soft-drive on the ceiling: the honest lesson is that the mask (hard) preserves ratio and phase and is idempotent, while the shift (soft) preserves only phase. Witness GREEN; tame_style_check bans clean. Next agent-doable Lotus lap: ALES89 infinite_clip into stereo (silence the quiet middle AND pin the loud to the rail) closes the dead-zone family, a clean finishing edge — a mechanical kg continuation.
